draw(E--F--G--H--cycle);
draw(I--J--K--L--cycle);
label("$P$", (2,2));
label("$Q$", (3,2));
label("$P^c \cap Q^c$", (1,1));
[/asy]

The number of boxes that contain pens or pencils is $|P \cup Q|$. By the principle of inclusion-exclusion,
\[|P \cup Q| = |P| + |Q| - |P \cap Q| = 5 + 4 - 2 = 7.\]Since there are ten boxes in total, the number of boxes that contain neither pens nor pencils is
\[|P^c \cap Q^c| = 10 - |P \cup Q| = 10 - 7 = \boxed{3}.\]

