\[AF^2 = AG^2 + GF^2 = \frac{4}{9} AD^2 + \frac{1}{4} AH^2.\]Similarly,
\[BF^2 = \frac{4}{9} BE^2 + \frac{1}{4} BH^2 \quad \text{and} \quad CF^2 = \frac{4}{9} CF^2 + \frac{1}{4} CH^2.\]Adding these equations, we get
\[AF^2 + BF^2 + CF^2 = \frac{4}{9} (AD^2 + BE^2 + CF^2) + \frac{1}{4} (AH^2 + BH^2 + CH^2).\]By the Pythagorean Theorem,
\[AD^2 + BE^2 + CF^2 = BC^2 + CA^2 + AB^2 = a^2 + b^2 + c^2.\]Also, by the Pythagorean Theorem,
\[AH^2 + BH^2 + CH^2 = 4R^2.\]Therefore,
\[AF^2 + BF^2 + CF^2 = \frac{4}{9} (a^2 + b^2 + c^2) + \frac{1}{4} (4R^2) = \frac{4}{9} (a^2 + b^2 + c^2) + R^2.\]

